-- title:
--   Rigidity of algebra maps from a finite étale algebra over a henselian local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a henselian local ring, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$. Let $E$ be a commutative $R$-algebra which is finite as an $R$-module and étale over $R$, and let $B$ be a commutative $R$-algebra which is finite as an $R$-module (no étaleness or flatness is assumed of $B$). Let $\varphi, \psi : E \to B$ be two $R$-algebra homomorphisms, and suppose that for every $x \in E$ the difference $\varphi(x) - \psi(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}$ under the structure map $R \to B$, i.e. in $\mathfrak{m}B$. The conclusion is that $\varphi = \psi$ as $R$-algebra maps. Note that $R$ is not assumed noetherian, so $\mathfrak{m}$ may equal $\mathfrak{m}^2$; the hypothesis is congruence modulo $\mathfrak{m}B$ rather than modulo a nilpotent or complete-adic ideal.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement for finite étale algebras over a henselian local ring: a morphism to a module-finite algebra is determined by its reduction modulo the maximal ideal (cf. EGA IV 18.5.11). It is used to obtain uniqueness of lifts of algebra and bialgebra maps along the residue field base change, and thereby that points of an étale quotient of a finite flat group scheme are determined by their residues.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_Etale_algHom_ext_of_forall_sub_mem_map_maximalIdeal_of_henselianLocalRing.lean

